from pathlib import Path
import ast,json,hashlib,shutil,markdown
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];O=R/'doc/research/possible-bodies';E=R/'doc/space/ca-proximity-review-2026-09-13';RUN=R/'ada_run/ca-proximity-review-2026-09-13';M=R/'commons/maps/CA_ExpandingSpace'
def sha(p):return hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
def save(p,s):
 p.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);t=p.with_name(p.name+'.tmp');t.write_bytes((s.strip()+'\n').encode());t.replace(p)
receipt=json.loads((RUN/'run.json').read_text())
assert receipt['exit']==0 and not receipt['failures'] and receipt['sources_unchanged']
assert all(sha(R/p)==v for p,v in receipt['source_sha256'].items()),'Capture sources have changed'
engine=(RUN/'CA_ExpandingSpace/engine.log').read_text(encoding='utf-8',errors='replace')
assert 'SCRIPT ERROR:' not in engine and 'Parse Error:' not in engine,'Runtime script errors block publication'
result=json.loads((RUN/'CA_ExpandingSpace/probe_ca_proximity_live.json').read_text())
for name in ['entrance','depleted','controls','readout','frieze','whole-hall']:shutil.copy2(RUN/f'CA_ExpandingSpace/{name}.png',O/f'ca-proximity-{name}.png')
for name in ['final','technical','critical','tutorial','field_notes']:shutil.copy2(M/f'{name}.md',O/f'ca-proximity-{name}.md')
shutil.copy2(R/'tools/ca_proximity_model.js',O/'ca-proximity-model.js')
save(E/'runtime-receipt.json',json.dumps(receipt,indent=2));save(E/'runtime-verification.json',json.dumps(result,indent=2))
tree=ast.parse((R/'tools/build_ca_history_review.py').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
css=next(ast.literal_eval(n.value) for n in tree.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='css' for t in n.targets))
css+='''.outputs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:150px minmax(0,1fr);gap:30px;align-items:start;margin:25px 0}.outputs svg{width:100%;display:block}.instrument{padding:18px;background:#203e43;border-left:3px solid #ffcc70}#witness{color:#ffdc97;font-weight:600}.prompt{padding:18px 22px;background:#203e43;border-radius:7px}.reading h1{font-size:40px}@media(max-width:600px){.outputs{grid-template-columns:100px minmax(0,1fr);gap:15px}.outputs h3{font-size:15px}}'''
body=markdown.markdown((M/'final.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8'),extensions=['fenced_code'])
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The surface includes you · Ada Research</title><style>__CSS__</style></head><body><main><nav><a href="learning-ladder.html">← Pedagogical ladder</a><a href="ca-life-addresses.html">Previous: a pattern visits an address</a><a href="/necklace/thread?map=CA_ExpandingSpace&role=primary">Primary &amp; book</a></nav><div class="eyebrow">Cellular automata / CA_ExpandingSpace</div><h1>The surface includes you</h1><p class="lead">A tile can still be visible after it stops carrying you. What enters the calculation when a visitor approaches?</p><p class="status">Implemented in Godot · __CHECKS__ desktop checks passed, including a body losing support and climbing back out. All seven artifacts remain. Headset and retained-gallery review remain for later.</p><figure><img src="ca-proximity-depleted.png" alt="Actual Godot museum: a mint bridge has a transparent depleted patch above a shallow basin, and the same patch appears on a wall frieze"><figcaption>Actual Godot capture. The nominated probe has depleted the marked region after 2.5 simulated seconds. The faint tiles remain visible; their support has been disabled.</figcaption></figure><section><h2>Approach, wait, withdraw</h2><p>Start with a full bridge. Let the pink probe stand in for you, then make your own position the input. The witness names health, distance, supporting collision and healthy neighbours. The wall wears the same state; it does not carry the same collision.</p><div class="gallery"><figure><img src="ca-proximity-entrance.png" alt="The full bridge above its collecting basin with a matching unbroken wall frieze"><figcaption>The restored beginning. A stable museum route continues beside the basin; two wedges on its left side let a body climb out.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="ca-proximity-controls.png" alt="Eight tilted controls below a large cased witness readout"><figcaption>STEP/RUN/RESTORE and input controls come first. CHAIN, ORDER and REVERSE expose the timing choice after the proximity encounter.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section id="experiment"><h2>Try the field remotely</h2><p class="small">This browser model uses the same eighty-cell rule and two nominated probe positions. Godot additionally tracks the visitor. The diagrams show health and its mappings; actual collision, body movement and headset reach require the game.</p><p class="prompt">Run with PROBE NEAR. Watch W lose health. Move NEAR/FAR and let recovery arrive from the cells that remain healthy. Then try the prepared CHAIN and compare one step under SYNC and SCAN.</p><div class="controls"><button id="step">STEP</button><button id="run" aria-pressed="false">RUN</button><button id="restore">RESTORE</button><button id="source" aria-pressed="true">INPUT</button><button id="near" aria-pressed="true">NEAR/FAR</button><button id="chain">CHAIN</button><button id="order" aria-pressed="true">ORDER</button><button id="reverse" aria-pressed="false">REVERSE</button></div><div class="instrument"><p id="status" role="status"></p><p id="witness"></p><p class="small" id="chain-values"></p></div><div class="outputs"><article><h3>A path</h3><div id="plane"></div></article><article><h3>The same state, worn by a wall</h3><div id="wall"></div><p id="support-count" class="small"></p><p class="small">Recovery neighbours: above 0.50.<br>Support: at least 0.20.<br>A tile at 0.30 can carry a body while contributing nothing to a neighbour’s recovery.</p></article></div><details><summary>How to compare the loop fairly</summary><p>CHAIN prepares 0.600, 0.495 and 0.000 at three adjacent addresses, with other cells depleted and external input disabled. One forward SCAN step lets the third cell rise to 0.010. In reverse SCAN it stays at zero. SYNC gives the same next field in both directions.</p><p>ORDER and REVERSE restore the current beginning. They do not reverse time. INPUT toggles the probe’s influence without resetting the field. RESTORE returns to the full beginning while retaining the other choices. The local clock holds after 300 updates.</p></details></section><section><h2>The red thread: a value gains consequences</h2><p>The history bridge mapped occupancy to support. Life connected a fixed cell to a lamp. Here proximity enters a graded state, whose thresholds control participation and support, while its colours dress a wall.</p><p>The new question is also about time. A neighbour’s new value can become available during this pass or on the next one. The same formula can inhabit different schedules. That choice belongs in the source, the room and the book.</p></section><section><details><summary>Read the revised book passage</summary><div class="reading">__BODY__</div></details></section><section><details><summary>See the whole hall and verification</summary><figure><img src="ca-proximity-frieze.png" alt="The shared health field shown in a framed wall frieze beside the bridge"></figure><figure><img src="ca-proximity-whole-hall.png" alt="Actual overhead museum view of the new proximity bay and the retained rear collection"><figcaption>The bridge now has its own bay. The original automatic hall removed crossway_ca to reopen its route; authored placement retains all seven works. The rear encounters need their own review.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="ca-proximity-readout.png" alt="A close view of the health, support, distance and update schedule instrument"></figure><p>__CHECKS__ actual Godot checks cover the museum walker and active desktop body, proximity and recovery, matched update directions, health thresholds, material sharing, eight pointer controls, support and ramp rays, a falling body, a climbed recovery ramp and an independent margin walk. No runtime script errors. Existing startup UID and catalyst viewport-texture diagnostics remain recorded separately.</p><p><a href="ca-proximity-technical.md">Technical account</a> · <a href="ca-proximity-critical.md">Critical text</a> · <a href="ca-proximity-field_notes.md">Field notes</a> · <a href="ca-proximity-verification.json">Verification</a></p></details></section><footer class="small"><a href="ca-proximity-final.md">Book source</a> · Next: CA_SoftRules. Build the live field before claiming what richer neighbourhood exchange can do.</footer></main><script src="ca-proximity-model.js"></script></body></html>'''
